// RtOp, json: `std.json`: building, reading, encoding and decoding. Read by `compiler/kir/build.rs`.
/// `std.json` (spec 2.12): parsing can fail, like `parse`.
JsonParse,
JsonStringify,
/// `json.of(value)`: the value comes in a one-item tuple, whose type
/// tells the runtime how to encode it.
JsonOf,
/// `json.decode<T>` and `json.decode_value<T>`: they can fail. The
/// third operand holds the defaults of record fields
/// (`runtime/native/src/rt_json_decode.rs`).
JsonDecode,
JsonDecodeValue,
/// Reading a `Json` (decision 0032): `j[key]`, `j[i]` and the methods
/// of `stdlib/json/json.kav` named after them, which on a parsed
/// document read its tape (`runtime/native/src/rt_json_read.rs`).
/// `JsonIntOr` and `JsonFloatOr` are `j.int() ?? fallback` and
/// `j.float() ?? fallback` for a fallback that costs nothing to
/// compute, with nothing boxed.
JsonGet,
JsonAt,
JsonList,
JsonObject,
JsonInt,
JsonFloat,
JsonText,
JsonBool,
JsonIsNull,
JsonLen,
JsonIntOr,
JsonFloatOr,
/// Before a `json.decode` (spec 2.12, decision 0086): records of type
/// number `a` are checked by closure `b` (`fn(T) -> Int`, the bits of
/// the invariants broken), whose invariants' texts are list `c`.
JsonCheckRegister,
